WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.350
Skill, plugin, agent, harness!

00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:06.930
There have never been more ways to extend your AI.

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:09.570
And nothing tells you which one fits the job.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:14.070
Too big, and it's refunding strangers at three in the morning.

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:17.710
Too small, and it breaks on the first odd email.

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:21.550
Pick wrong, and your customers find out before you do.

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:24.930
Every AI idea starts the same way.

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:26.990
An agent, by Friday, please!

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:27.990
Hold on.

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:30.630
One word just answered three questions.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:33.310
What form it takes.

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:34.970
How much it does on its own.

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:36.970
What kind of AI it needs.

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:40.230
Right Shape answers all three.

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:41.790
You just describe the job.

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:50.750
Take a support inbox that refunds small orders.

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:52.490
It wants to run on its own.

00:00:54.460 --> 00:00:56.550
But it reads strangers' email.

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:58.150
And it moves money!

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:04.170
So it lands on rung five, right alongside you, until the refund limit is set in code.

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:07.350
Then it writes a test you can actually fail.

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:08.850
A trap to catch.

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:10.810
A case to leave alone.

00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:15.390
Most of the time, the right shape is smaller than you think.

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:21.290
Right Shape.

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:24.570
The easy way to extend your AI, the right way.
